github.com/users/yamen-haddad","html_url":"https://github.com/yamen-haddad","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yamen-haddad/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-01-26T23:32:11Z","updated_at":"2023-01-26T23:32:11Z","body":"As @ttyusupov said, when using the option `--print_entries=pb`, the WAL entry is being printed using the `DebugString()` of `google::protobuf::Message` class. Which prints the object without decoding the fields of type `bytes` and the `transaction_id ` is of type `bytes` and hence it is printed this way.\r\nIn this case, maybe we cannot use the `DebugString()` of protobuf and instead have our own implementation for it which should traverse recursively all the fields/subfields in the `LogEntryPB ` object. The problem with that solution is that it will be coupled with the current structure of `LogEntryPB` message and any change on the message definition might cause the new function to break. I am not sure if this is the best way to move forward or you propose something else?\r\ncc @rthallamko3 ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/1405812566/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"yamen